msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:13
msgid ""
"The following example shows how to write a http echo server that delays "
"its response by 1000 ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:30
msgid ""
"If you are not using `Stream#pipe`, you can also manually release the "
"buffered events by calling `delayedStream.resume()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:42
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:44
msgid ""
"In order to use this meta stream properly, here are a few things you "
"should know about the implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:47
msgid "Event Buffering / Proxying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:49
msgid ""
"All events of the `source` stream are hijacked by overwriting the "
"`source.emit` method. Until node implements a catch-all event listener, "
"this is the only way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:52
msgid ""
"However, delayed-stream still continues to emit all events it captures on"
" the `source`, regardless of whether you have released the delayed stream"
" yet or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:56
msgid ""
"Upon creation, delayed-stream captures all `source` events and stores "
"them in an internal event buffer. Once `delayedStream.release()` is "
"called, all buffered events are emitted on the `delayedStream`, and the "
"event buffer is cleared. After that, delayed-stream merely acts as a "
"proxy for the underlaying source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:62
msgid "Error handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:64
msgid ""
"Error events on `source` are buffered / proxied just like any other "
"events. However, `delayedStream.create` attaches a no-op `'error'` "
"listener to the `source`. This way you only have to handle errors on the "
"`delayedStream` object, rather than in two places."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:69
msgid "Buffer limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:71
msgid ""
"delayed-stream provides a `maxDataSize` property that can be used to "
"limit the amount of data being buffered. In order to protect you from bad"
" `source` streams that don't react to `source.pause()`, this feature is "
"enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:76
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:78
msgid "DelayedStream.create(source, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:80
msgid "Returns a new `delayedStream`. Available options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:82
msgid "`pauseStream`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:83
msgid "`maxDataSize`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:85
msgid "The description for those properties can be found below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:87
msgid "delayedStream.source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:89
msgid ""
"The `source` stream managed by this object. This is useful if you are "
"passing your `delayedStream` around, and you still want to access "
"properties on the `source` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:93
msgid "delayedStream.pauseStream = true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:95
msgid ""
"Whether to pause the underlaying `source` when calling "
"`DelayedStream.create()`. Modifying this property afterwards has no "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:98
msgid "delayedStream.maxDataSize = 1024 * 1024"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:100
msgid "The amount of data to buffer before emitting an `error`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:102
msgid ""
"If the underlaying source is emitting `Buffer` objects, the `maxDataSize`"
" refers to bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:105
msgid ""
"If the underlaying source is emitting JavaScript strings, the size refers"
" to characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:108
msgid ""
"If you know what you are doing, you can set this property to `Infinity` "
"to disable this feature. You can also modify this property during "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:111
msgid "delayedStream.dataSize = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:113
msgid "The amount of data buffered so far."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:115
msgid "delayedStream.readable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:117
msgid "An ECMA5 getter that returns the value of `source.readable`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:119
msgid "delayedStream.resume()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:121
msgid ""
"If the `delayedStream` has not been released so far, "
"`delayedStream.release()` is called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:124
msgid "In either case, `source.resume()` is called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:126
msgid "delayedStream.pause()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:128
msgid "Calls `source.pause()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:130
msgid "delayedStream.pipe(dest)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:132
msgid ""
"Calls `delayedStream.resume()` and then proxies the arguments to "
"`source.pipe`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:134
msgid "delayedStream.release()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/delayed-stream_Readme.md:136
msgid ""
"Emits and clears all events that have been buffered up so far. This does "
"not resume the underlaying source, use `delayedStream.resume()` instead."
msgstr ""

